  :doc/body
  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 11

WIP=1 after iteration 10 was the leftover on the published runner: call plus
fuel-on-entry. Self-tail past the prologue does not help 100k C calls — each
call is a new entry. This iteration removes the charge from entries that
cannot re-enter.

## What was actually there

`emit-program` prefixed **every** function with the fuel prologue
(`ldr x16,[x7,#8]` / `cmp qword [r9+8],0`). `kexe-benchmark.c` then stored
`context.fuel = 512` before every invoke because 100k decrements exceed 512.
The kernel was a straight-line leaf. Fuel does not bound it. The host loop
does.

`compile-kir-module` without prefixes never had that prefix, which is why the
encoding tests (1 MUL + 8 MADD) were green while the timed artifact still
paid 20 bytes and two memory ops per call.

## The change

`entry-fuel-prefixes` looks at lowered GMIR. Charge only when a function
contains `:gmir/call`, `:gmir/tail-call`, `:gmir/runtime-call`, or
`:gmir/capability-call`. Arithmetic, `if`, `let`, and `do` omit it.

Break / unbreak, both ISAs:

- acyclic `(+ (* n 48271) 1)` via `emit-program` does **not** start with the
  fuel instruction. Putting the prefix back on every name turns this red.
- `(if (< n 1) n (down (- n 1)))` **does** start with it. Skipping every name
  turns this red, and a 512-deep countdown would no longer trap.

ADR-0034. kotoba-native `d4b050ae`. West pin `c15026ff` → `d4b050ae`
(superproject `03ac006f`). Do not bump amu without perfgate.

## Encoding of the production bytes

`kernel_wide` through JVM `clojure -M:run compile` with this native:

| | before | after |
|---|---:|---:|
| bytes | 576 | **556** |
| first insn | `ldr x16,[x7,#8]` | `movz` of 48271 |
| MUL / MADD | 1 / 8 | 1 / 8 |

Dump: `/tmp/kernel-wide-leaf-fuel/`.

## What this does not close

- LLVM still inlines into the timed loop. amu still calls `kexe_fn8`.
- `kexe-benchmark.c` still stores fuel every call. For this leaf that store
  is now dead; recursive exports still need a remaining count.
- The call / all-vreg path is unchanged (iteration 8).
- No timed ranking. Iteration 10 was loadavg 24. Seal only via
  `kotoba-lang/perfgate`, this kernel, min quantile, 25 rotated samples.

Do not land fused-srem, extra MOV peepholes, FMA, PGO, a kototama optimizer,
or a timed `bench` export. Do not overwrite iterations 04–10. Do not claim
LLVM beaten."}]
